# Response headers for statically-served files, for hosts that honour a
# Cloudflare-style _headers file (Cloudflare's assets binding applies it to
# requests it serves without running the Worker - `vite preview` does, for
# example; vinext writes an auto-generated version of this file only when one
# is NOT already present, so this one is kept as-is). The server-rendered
# documents are generated BY the Worker, not served from here; their headers
# are set in code - see worker/security-headers.ts.
#
# NOTE (checked 2026-10-07): the current production host does NOT apply this
# file. Static responses on vedasaarathi.com carry none of the headers below,
# and /_headers is itself served as a downloadable file. It is kept because
# it is correct for hosts that do honour it; see
# docs/temp/security-privacy-licensing-review-2026-10-07.md.
#
# Do not add a Content-Security-Policy here: it is set once, in
# worker/security-headers.ts, where its exact requirements are documented
# next to it. Two independently-maintained copies would drift.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
